  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message as the target of gun control policy",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the audience of the meme, who are framed as 'innocent people' who are being targeted by political leaders to surrender their guns. The text 'leaders want innocent people to give up their guns' directly addresses the user as part of the group being affected by gun control policies, making the user a subject of the political narrative presented. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'your', but the phrasing 'innocent people' creates an inclusive projection where the viewer identifies with the group being threatened, thus projecting themselves as the 'innocent people' in the meme's narrative.",
